  message: "Fixed in PR #1534 (merged as 73e0340f35 + f6d33da9ef). Root cause: _collect_config_content iterated the frozenset _MONOREPO_MANIFEST_NAMES and unsorted globs; _collect_config_content_with_discovery iterated the 'discovered' set and unsorted *-pattern globs; _discover_config_files_embedding/_get_repo_languages iterated a set and unsorted rglob fallbacks. The 15-file cap and first-come cross-file dedup turned that order into which files the section shows. Fix: _MONOREPO_MANIFEST_NAMES is a tuple in CONFIG_FILES order; per-kind matches sorted (mirrors the heuristic); every set/glob/rglob in the path sorted. Also: discovery compared unresolved paths against resolved seen_paths, double-listing manifests under a relative root (40 entries for 32 files) - now resolved. Cap pragma removed (exercised by test). Evidence (CLI, fresh XDG_CACHE_HOME per run, 6-service mixed-config fixture, hybrid default): pre-fix 51f5b3755f seeds 0/1/2 -> Configuration sha256 9facdaec0a07ab8e / e0921160e93e9e76 / bc66e0a1663c6824; dev f6d33da9ef seeds 0/1/2 -> 7f29c2e710bc99a8 x3. Filed repro (_extract_config_embedding on 32-manifest fixture, PYTHONHASHSEED 0/1/2): pre-fix 73a70b68541a / 89e9f25a2012 / 6c652c26a909 (three file sets); dev 184036bb508a x3, collect list 53fc80bc57ad x3. Tests: test_config_section_determinism.py (salted subprocess runs of candidate list and embedding output, cap test, order contracts, dedup)."  # d2be
